{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgh69aCL8LywNRAD2vXjz", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**Answer:** Two services take payments directly: **OrderService** and **RenewalsWorker**. Both call **PaymentsAPI**. One caveat comes first.\n\n**Caveat:** A direct lookup on **PaymentsService** finds nothing that depends on it, even at 4 hops. Callers point at **PaymentsAPI**, not at the service itself. The graph has no edge saying PaymentsService serves PaymentsAPI. I'm assuming it does, based on the name. If that's wrong, the graph shows no service that would be affected by a PaymentsService outage, and the link needs adding to the graph.\n\n**Services that can no longer take payments (direct callers of PaymentsAPI):**\n- **OrderService**: `OrderService -CALLS-> PaymentsAPI`. Customers can't pay for orders.\n- **RenewalsWorker**: `RenewalsWorker -CALLS-> PaymentsAPI`. Subscription renewals can't be charged.\n\n**Services that depend on OrderService, so may be degraded but don't take payments themselves:**\n- **BillingService**: `DEPENDS_ON -> OrderService`\n- **ReportingService**: `DEPENDS_ON -> OrderService`\n- **SearchService**: `DEPENDS_ON -> OrderService`\n\n**What PaymentsService depends on:**\n- **NotificationsAPI** (CALLS). Payment-related notifications would stop. BillingService also calls NotificationsAPI directly, so its own notifications aren't affected.\n- **PaymentsPostgresDatabase** (STORES). No new payment records would be written while the service is down.\n\n**Configuration keys:** I didn't trace any, because the question didn't name one and the graph lookups didn't turn any up."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 716, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4684, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 716}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "7526ef51-d541-442a-9fef-65caaff12158", "uuid": "91dba4b8-e84d-4a90-b6c6-43a015178d07", "timestamp": "2026-11-04T02:21:15.262Z", "request_id": "req_011Cgh69ZxwmxZLFCF8Zypig"}
